<title>UK: Kingfisher details senior appointments.</title>
<headline>Kingfisher details senior appointments.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>British retailer Kingfisher Plc said on Friday that Jim Glover, currently deputy managing director of its Woolworths subsidiary, had been appointed managing director of Superdrug.</p>
<p>The appointment follows the resignation of Graham Steele for personal reasons. Glover assumes his new role on August 26.</p>
<p>Roger Holmes, B&amp;Q's finance systems and supply chain director, takes over from Glover at Woolworths immediately and will then assume the role of managing director in the spring of 1998 when Roger Jones retires.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
